<title>USA: General Employment Q2 March 31 net rises.</title>
<headline>General Employment Q2 March 31 net rises.</headline>
<dateline>OAKBROOK TERRACE, Ill. 1997-04-22</dateline>
<text>
<p>Three Months  Six Months</p>
<p>					 Ended March 31  Ended March 31</p>
<p>					   1997    1996    1997    1996</p>
<p> Net revenues			 $7,326 $5,804 $13,230 $10,801</p>
<p>Costs and expenses:</p>
<p>   Cost of services(A)	     5,202  4,116   9,484   7,751</p>
<p>   General and administrative	999  1,022   1,917   1,870</p>
<p> Income before income taxes	1,125    666   1,829   1,180</p>
<p> Provision for income taxes	  450    265     730     465</p>
<p> Net income				675    401   1,099     715</p>
<p> Net income per share(B)	     .25    .15     .41     .27</p>
<p> Average number of shares(B)     2,675  2,623   2,676   2,623</p>
<p>		   (In Thousands, Except Per Share)</p>
<p>(A) -- The 1996 periods include a $144,000 pretax gain resulting from a renegotiation of the company's corporate headquarters office lease.</p>
<p>(B) -- Share and per share amounts have been adjusted to reflect a 15 percent stock dividend paid November 1, 1996. NOTE: Full company name is General Employment Enterprises Inc.</p>
<p>((--Chicago newsdesk, 312-408-8787))</p>
